{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/20","id":4514786765,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUSya2c8AAAABDRotzQ","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/20","diff_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/20.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pull/20.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/issues/20","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/20/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/20/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/issues/20/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader/statuses/2144c358c2b41aa235b15cf0fa472289aec8673f","number":20,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add arithmetic sum-fibre connection and the conormal trace morphism","user":{"login":"KokunoYumeto","id":208192274,"node_id":"U_kgDODGjDEg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208192274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Additive continuation of #17\n\nBase: `33b29f706008124886614ba4bd55bffc489df9e2`.\nHead: `2144c358c2b41aa235b15cf0fa472289aec8673f`.\n\nFive added files under `workbenches/tau-sum-connection/`. No existing mathematics, original scalar construction, formalization, dependency, workflow or other-session branch is modified. Draft for review, not a merge.\n\n## New analytic estimate on the actual sum pushforward\n\nFor the retained reflection-stable arithmetic input `a_h(t)=(g/h)(1/2+it)/sqrt(2pi)`, `g=2xi`, keep the full mass `mu_h=int |a_h|^2`. Construct the product amplitude over the centered sum coordinate, its line projection and its normal derivative. Prove\n\n`I_(h,k) + 4 int ||n_k(u)||^2 du = mu_h^(k-1) I_h / k`,\n\nwhere `I_h=4||log(x)F_h||^2` and `I_(h,k)=int (m_k')^2/m_k` for the actual convolution density. No probability mass is assigned one, no log-concavity is assumed, and zeros are handled with the smooth amplitude rather than an everywhere-defined logarithmic score. This is the Fisher-information projection mechanism with its full arithmetic and relative data retained, not a claim of a new general convolution inequality.\n\n## Full relative matrix and its arithmetic derivative\n\nConstruct the fibre injection j(u), metric W=j*j, connection Gamma=W^(-1)j*j', and normal map N=(1-jW^(-1)j*)j'. Prove the full orthogonal derivative decomposition, metric compatibility and N*N=T-B*W^(-1)B. Fixed arithmetic phase gives B=W'/2. A changing relative frame retains the extra C^(-1)C' term. The actual degree-filtered graph is retained before taking arithmetic jets.\n\nThe derivative is explicitly linked to the original generator by the Mellin isometry and `[D_tot,(1/k)sum log x_i]=-1`. It is not substituted for scaling.\n\n## The new e-sensitive map into the old Jacobian trace\n\nFor the exact relation ideal I=(h(s_1),...,h(s_k)), construct the original split quotient of P/I^2 onto P/I and its conormal kernel I/I^2. The sum derivative descends from that larger domain, with exact conormal row `(a_i) -> (1/k)sum h'(s_i)a_i`. The quotient is a ring map; the derivative is a coefficient-linear map. Both preserve tau and supported zero. A nonzero conormal relation can become e under the quotient while its derivative remains nonzero.\n\nCarry the actual Taylor unit U=prod(g/h) through the derivative. In one variable the resulting source equation is\n\n`J_h(log(x) Theta(phi)) = j_h(g') j_h(H_phi)`.\n\nPairing with the existing residue form gives the arithmetic multiplication trace, with the original factor 2, local units and multiplicities. All higher I-adic layers and the product Jacobian are computed, retaining the original tensor signs.\n\n## Coordination and evidence\n\nThe new Kernel Layer Integration upload is identical to its earlier copy. All 31+53 entries of the two inspected source manifests verified. Its 18-method suite passed fresh normal and optimized reruns. This does not enlarge the parallel session's Lean certificate.\n\nThe new public checker has 20 exact finite methods. Normal and optimized runs passed with identical success JSON; both deliberately failing controls failed. Published note and checker blobs match the local files. The expanded conversation package includes the full HTML/LaTeX derivation, source receipts, reader checks, and a two-precision numerical evaluation of the actual theta seed. The numerical evaluation is not an interval certificate.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo uniform sublinear bound for the source's full finite-packet weight-control matrices has been proved here. The scalar sum-density contraction is not assigned to every relative polynomial direction. The full connection, normal matrix, filtered graph and conormal response specify the remaining comparison. No new Lean execution, finite-field purity transfer, RH or GRH proof is claimed.\n\nOnly authored mathematical exposition, checking code and bounded verification metadata are published; no private transcript or external source corpus.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-12T18:31:12Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T18:31:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d4d7b065beb0d9f52cf30f9e3e513dfe38859a77","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"KokunoYumeto:polyclank/tau-sum-connection-20260912","ref":"polyclank/tau-sum-connection-20260912","repo":{"id":1361877721,"node_id":"R_kgDOUSya2Q","name":"zeta-function-research-reader","full_name":"KokunoYumeto/zeta-function-research-reader","owner":{"login":"KokunoYumeto","id":208192274,"node_id":"U_kgDODGjDEg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/208192274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto","html_url":"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KokunoYumeto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Living literature-based zeta research reader: complete TeX proofs, references, calculations and exploratory Navier-Stokes, heat, arithmetic-trace and geometric-complexity workbenches.","homepage":